+// The collection a text label should name as this item's origin. On an
+// aggregate page -- Favorites is assembled from .sub files -- a game's
+// collection differs from the page showing it, and the page name ("Favorites")
+// says nothing. Everywhere else the item's collection is the page's own, so
+// the page name is already right. leaf excludes menu entries: their
+// collectionInfo is the menu collection itself today, and if a future menu
+// builder ever points it at the target, a highlighted system's name must
+// still not replace the page's.
+std::string Item::owningCollectionName(const std::string &pageCollection) const
+{
+    if(leaf && collectionInfo && collectionInfo->name != pageCollection)
+    {
+        return collectionInfo->name;
+    }
+    return pageCollection;
+}
